Subject: Preserve the declared order of union enumeration types

Management-common's generated bindings must keep the YANG union's declared
subtype order. Iterating a Go map can reorder the generated reflection map,
for example from declared ZULU, ALPHA to ALPHA, ZULU. Sort by the recorded
declaration index, using names only to break equal indices.
The shared owner's union-order regression exercises this generator output.

Origin: Unmodified diff from sonic-mgmt-common's
patches/0003-ygot-preserve-union-enum-order.patch at merged commit
f5361ba8b88cde7ec59bdb4652a986c68d66da64:
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-mgmt-common/blob/f5361ba8b88cde7ec59bdb4652a986c68d66da64/patches/0003-ygot-preserve-union-enum-order.patch

